WEBVTT

00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:08.680
So, why were you rolling around
in Cyprion cactus?

00:00:08.725 --> 00:00:10.693
You know Rebecca Smith?

00:00:10.727 --> 00:00:12.695
The new Tactical officer?

00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:14.754
We took a walk in the arboretum.

00:00:14.798 --> 00:00:16.823
We sat down,
we got comfortable.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:20.325
Things got a little romantic,
and then I rolled over.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.337
Ow!

00:00:21.371 --> 00:00:23.134
Blurred vision and dizziness

00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:25.698
uh, palpitations...

00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:29.200
a stinging sensation
in the lower spine.

00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:32.044
It's Terellian Death Syndrome,
isn't it?

00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:34.141
I thought we agreed
you'd come to me

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:36.709
before checking
Starfleet Medical Database.

00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:38.914
Yes, well, this time,
I'm glad I did.

00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:41.354
Because maybe we can stop
the cellular decay

00:00:41.391 --> 00:00:42.915
before it's too late.

00:00:42.993 --> 00:00:45.723
Reg, you don't have
Terellian Death Syndrome.

00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:47.696
Are you... you're sure?

00:00:47.731 --> 00:00:48.959
I'm sure.

00:00:53.236 --> 00:00:56.205
Then maybe it is
Symbalene Blood Burn.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:58.639
No. No.

00:00:58.675 --> 00:01:01.735
I don't see anything
wrong with you at all.

00:01:01.778 --> 00:01:03.177
Wait a minute.

00:01:03.213 --> 00:01:06.614
There is a slight imbalance
in your K-3 cell count.

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.878
My K-3s? Oh, no.

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:11.352
Barclay, I'm sure it's nothing.

00:01:11.388 --> 00:01:14.880
Look, I'll run
a microcellular scan.

00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:16.254
We'll see.

00:01:16.293 --> 00:01:18.193
This will take
a couple of minutes.

00:01:18.228 --> 00:01:20.526
Nurse Baldwin, I need
that hemotoxin series

00:01:20.564 --> 00:01:22.122
on Ensign Brooks right away.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:28.304
How's my
smallest patient doing?

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:30.033
I believe she is doing well.

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.064
Her appetite has increased
by seven percent

00:01:32.109 --> 00:01:35.408
and she is beginning to engage
in prenatal behavior.

00:01:35.445 --> 00:01:37.003
Oh, she is getting close.

00:01:37.047 --> 00:01:39.641
You'll have a fresh litter
of hungry kittens

00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:41.207
before the week is over.

00:01:41.251 --> 00:01:42.616
Let me just run an amniotic scan

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:44.017
to make sure
everything's fine...

00:01:44.054 --> 00:01:45.021
Doctor?

00:01:45.055 --> 00:01:46.113
And then I'II...

00:01:46.156 --> 00:01:48.852
Doctor, my capillaries
are shrinking.

00:01:48.892 --> 00:01:50.416
Excuse me.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.520
Alyssa, can you take care
of Spot for a minute?

00:01:53.563 --> 00:01:55.758
Start a preliminary
amniotic scan.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:57.391
Yes, Doctor.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.901
My intravascular pressure...

00:01:58.935 --> 00:02:00.903
it's going through the roof.

00:02:00.937 --> 00:02:02.632
You're right.
It is elevated.

00:02:02.672 --> 00:02:05.971
You've also got heightened
electrophoretic activity.

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:07.874
Electrophoretic activity.

00:02:07.944 --> 00:02:09.241
Is it serious?

00:02:09.279 --> 00:02:12.373
Well, based on this,
I'd say you've got...

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:13.883
70, maybe 80 years.

00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:15.407
80...

00:02:15.452 --> 00:02:17.044
80 years?

00:02:17.087 --> 00:02:18.384
Yes, Reg.

00:02:18.422 --> 00:02:22.358
What you've got is a mild case
of Urodelean flu.

00:02:22.392 --> 00:02:23.689
Now, it's nothing serious.

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.718
Most humans have
a natural immunity to it.

00:02:25.762 --> 00:02:27.286
But the T cell in your DNA

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.026
that would normally fight off
the infection is dormant.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.125
Hmm.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:32.692
So, you mean, I have bad genes.

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:36.228
You have one dormant gene
out of 100,000

00:02:36.273 --> 00:02:39.765
and I can activate that gene
with a synthetic T cell

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.075
to let the body
fight the infection naturally.

00:02:43.113 --> 00:02:45.741
You should feel better
in a couple of days.

00:02:45.782 --> 00:02:47.249
Thank you, Doctor.

00:02:47.284 --> 00:02:49.411
I feel much-much better.

00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:51.080
Good!

00:02:51.121 --> 00:02:54.284
Now, stay away
from Medical Database.

00:02:56.226 --> 00:02:58.217
And you stay out
of the arboretum.

00:02:59.863 --> 00:03:01.660
Everything looks fine, Data.

00:03:01.698 --> 00:03:04.292
You want to know
the sex of the kittens?

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:07.269
I have noticed that many humans
prefer not to know

00:03:07.304 --> 00:03:10.205
in order to experience
the surprise during birth.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.141
I believe I will preserve
the mystery until then.

00:03:13.176 --> 00:03:15.144
I know what you mean.

00:03:15.178 --> 00:03:17.544
I don't want to know either.

00:03:17.581 --> 00:03:18.639
Alyssa?

00:03:18.682 --> 00:03:21.879
Spot's not the only one
who's going to be a mother.

00:03:21.918 --> 00:03:23.783
Oh, Alyssa, that's wonderful!

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.720
How did Andrew take the news?

00:03:25.755 --> 00:03:28.883
He was a little shocked,
but he's getting over it.

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:32.588
I have spent the past nine weeks
as an expectant parent.

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:35.621
I would be happy to share
my insights with your husband.

00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:37.462
If my experience
is any indication

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.731
he will need all the help
he can get.

00:04:07.964 --> 00:04:12.367
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:12.402 --> 00:04:16.236
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:04:16.273 --> 00:04:18.241
Its continuing mission...

00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:22.211
to explore strange new worlds

00:04:22.245 --> 00:04:26.682
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:04:26.716 --> 00:04:31.210
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:30.113 --> 00:05:33.605
Captain's Log, Stardate 47653.2.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:34.981
We are performing field tests

00:05:35.018 --> 00:05:38.010
of our new tactical systems
and weapon upgrades.

00:05:38.054 --> 00:05:41.080
Mr. Worf is supervising
the exercises.

00:05:41.124 --> 00:05:43.820
The next test will involve
the new photon torpedoes.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.851
The explosive yield
has been increased

00:05:45.895 --> 00:05:48.796
by 11%, and I

00:05:48.832 --> 00:05:51.426
have enhanced
the targeting system

00:05:51.468 --> 00:05:52.901
for increased accuracy.

00:05:53.003 --> 00:05:54.800
Sounds fascinating, Mr. Worf.

00:05:54.838 --> 00:05:56.135
Please proceed.

00:05:56.172 --> 00:05:58.640
Setting targeting coordinates...

00:05:58.675 --> 00:06:03.044
005 mark 317, spread
pattern delta 94.

00:06:03.079 --> 00:06:05.240
Torpedoes armed and loaded, sir.

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:06.806
Fire when ready.

00:06:13.156 --> 00:06:15.283
Worf?

00:06:17.294 --> 00:06:20.593
One of the torpedoes
has veered off course.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.760
It appears to be a malfunction
in the guidance system.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:27.861
Abort and destroy.

00:06:27.937 --> 00:06:29.871
The torpedo is not responding.

00:06:29.939 --> 00:06:32.874
Subspace detonator
will not engage.

00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:34.341
Lock on phasers.

00:06:34.377 --> 00:06:37.437
The torpedo is out of range.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.880
Even for your newly
improved phasers?

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:43.112
Maintain a sensor lock
on the torpedo, Mr. Worf.

00:06:43.153 --> 00:06:44.848
We'll have to go after it.

00:06:44.888 --> 00:06:46.685
That would be inadvisable, sir.

00:06:46.723 --> 00:06:48.884
The asteroid field
is unusually dense.

00:06:48.992 --> 00:06:52.428
The Enterprise is too large
to safely navigate through it.

00:06:52.462 --> 00:06:55.431
Then I'll take a shuttlecraft
and retrieve it.

00:06:55.465 --> 00:06:57.057
Mr. Data, you're with me.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.294
Captain, the shuttle pilot

00:06:58.335 --> 00:06:59.893
who's on duty
is Lieutenant Hayes.

00:06:59.936 --> 00:07:03.235
I happen to be a reasonably
qualified pilot, Number One.

00:07:03.273 --> 00:07:05.264
Besides, these tests
hardly require

00:07:05.308 --> 00:07:07.242
the Captain's
personal attention.

00:07:07.277 --> 00:07:08.505
Understood.

00:07:08.545 --> 00:07:10.376
Enjoy yourself.

00:07:10.413 --> 00:07:12.847
Mr. Worf...

00:07:12.882 --> 00:07:17.182
I think that you should
consider analyzing

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.745
your new guidance system.

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:22.849
Captain, I will need
a few minutes

00:07:22.959 --> 00:07:26.053
to attend
to a personal matter.

00:07:26.096 --> 00:07:27.757
Me?

00:07:27.797 --> 00:07:29.196
It is possible
that it will take

00:07:29.232 --> 00:07:30.961
several days
for Captain Picard and me

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.490
to complete our mission.

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.867
I would prefer to have
a human present

00:07:34.938 --> 00:07:37.065
to supervise
the birthing process.

00:07:37.107 --> 00:07:38.369
Well, I'd be honored.

00:07:38.408 --> 00:07:39.397
Yes... ooh.

00:07:41.745 --> 00:07:42.712
I have noticed

00:07:42.746 --> 00:07:45.442
that you are the only
other member of the crew

00:07:45.482 --> 00:07:47.279
whom Spot seems to like.

00:07:47.317 --> 00:07:49.615
Really?
That's hard to believe.

00:07:49.652 --> 00:07:52.143
You're such
a sweet little kitty.

00:07:52.188 --> 00:07:54.588
She is to you.

00:07:54.624 --> 00:07:56.854
However...

00:07:56.893 --> 00:08:00.852
there have been several injuries
to other members of the crew

00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:03.229
who have attempted
to care for Spot.

00:08:03.266 --> 00:08:05.826
So, has she, um...

00:08:05.935 --> 00:08:08.335
picked a place?

00:08:08.371 --> 00:08:10.737
A place?

00:08:10.774 --> 00:08:12.605
Cats usually like to pick

00:08:12.642 --> 00:08:15.008
a specific location
to give birth

00:08:15.044 --> 00:08:19.140
and it's usually
dark and secluded.

00:08:19.182 --> 00:08:21.616
And I believe...

00:08:21.651 --> 00:08:25.849
that this is...

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:27.686
it.

00:08:31.694 --> 00:08:34.254
I'm curious, sir.

00:08:34.297 --> 00:08:36.822
Who's the father?

00:08:36.866 --> 00:08:38.390
I am not certain.

00:08:38.435 --> 00:08:40.426
Spot has escaped
from my quarters

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.767
on several occasions

00:08:41.805 --> 00:08:44.137
and there are
12 male felines on board.

00:08:44.174 --> 00:08:47.268
I intend to run a full
DNA analysis on the kittens

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.607
once they...

00:08:48.645 --> 00:08:52.046
Picard to Data.
Report to Shuttle Bay Two.

00:08:52.081 --> 00:08:54.413
On my way, sir.

00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:55.884
Good-bye, Spot.

00:08:55.985 --> 00:08:58.886
I believe you are in good hands.

00:08:58.988 --> 00:09:02.048
You have nothing
to worry about, sir.

00:09:13.203 --> 00:09:15.262
Oh!

00:09:17.273 --> 00:09:18.672
Problem?

00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:22.109
I have performed 13 diagnostics
on the weapons array

00:09:22.145 --> 00:09:24.443
and I can find nothing wrong
with the guidance system.

00:09:24.481 --> 00:09:25.846
I'll have Geordi
run a diagnostic

00:09:25.882 --> 00:09:26.974
on the torpedo bay itself.

00:09:27.016 --> 00:09:28.176
Maybe he can find something.

00:09:28.218 --> 00:09:31.016
Must you stand so close to me?

00:09:31.054 --> 00:09:33.989
Lieutenant, are you all right?

00:09:34.023 --> 00:09:35.854
Yes, I'm fine.

00:09:35.925 --> 00:09:36.857
No, you're not.

00:09:36.926 --> 00:09:38.518
You've been working
for six hours straight.

00:09:38.561 --> 00:09:39.550
You're tired.
Take a break.

00:09:39.596 --> 00:09:40.688
But I...

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:42.061
That's an order, Lieutenant.

00:09:50.905 --> 00:09:52.873
Thanks for waiting.

00:09:52.907 --> 00:09:55.375
Do not approach me unannounced

00:09:55.409 --> 00:09:57.741
especially when I'm eating!

00:09:57.778 --> 00:10:00.747
We were supposed to be having
lunch together, remember?

00:10:00.781 --> 00:10:02.078
I was hungry!

00:10:02.116 --> 00:10:03.708
Well, I'm hungry, too.

00:10:03.751 --> 00:10:05.878
Excuse me.

00:10:05.953 --> 00:10:06.977
Yes?

00:10:07.021 --> 00:10:10.388
Could I have an order
of Ongilin caviar?

00:10:10.424 --> 00:10:12.289
Make that a double order.

00:10:12.326 --> 00:10:13.293
Certainly.

00:10:13.327 --> 00:10:14.521
Caviar?

00:10:14.562 --> 00:10:15.859
For lunch?

00:10:15.896 --> 00:10:18.729
I'm in the mood
for something salty.

00:10:18.766 --> 00:10:22.258
Besides, it's no stranger
than what you're eating.

00:10:31.011 --> 00:10:34.378
Have you noticed how dry
the air is on this ship?

00:10:34.415 --> 00:10:38.044
I wonder if the environmental
controls are set properly.

00:10:39.687 --> 00:10:41.917
You're excused.

00:10:42.022 --> 00:10:43.319
Here you go.

00:10:43.357 --> 00:10:44.915
Mmm.

00:10:59.039 --> 00:11:00.529
Is something wrong?

00:11:06.847 --> 00:11:09.077
It has been a difficult day.

00:11:09.116 --> 00:11:11.846
The torpedo
guidance system failed.

00:11:11.885 --> 00:11:13.182
It was my fault.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.279
You always say that.

00:11:15.322 --> 00:11:18.382
It was my fault!

00:11:18.425 --> 00:11:20.620
I designed that guidance system!

00:11:20.661 --> 00:11:22.993
Worf, calm down.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:27.694
I think you're under more stress
than you'd like to admit.

00:11:27.735 --> 00:11:30.670
Maybe you should
get some rest.

00:11:30.704 --> 00:11:33.264
Perhaps you are right.

00:11:33.307 --> 00:11:35.969
If you will excuse me!

00:11:37.978 --> 00:11:40.572
I didn't mean right now.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.578
We removed the torpedo bay's
primary guidance module

00:12:52.619 --> 00:12:53.916
and we found a power
fluctuation

00:12:54.021 --> 00:12:55.283
in the forward sensor cluster.

00:12:55.322 --> 00:12:57.153
Now, we think it may be
a radial imbalance

00:12:57.191 --> 00:12:58.317
in the phase discriminator.

00:12:58.358 --> 00:12:59.552
Now, what we want to do next

00:12:59.593 --> 00:13:00.787
is run a level-4 diagnostic

00:13:00.828 --> 00:13:02.261
but we're going
to have to shut down

00:13:02.296 --> 00:13:03.524
auxiliary power to 19 decks...

00:13:03.564 --> 00:13:04.531
Wait a minute.
Slow down.

00:13:04.565 --> 00:13:05.532
You lost me back there.

00:13:05.566 --> 00:13:06.533
Which sensor clusters?

00:13:06.567 --> 00:13:07.966
The forward.
It's...

00:13:08.001 --> 00:13:09.992
It's a power fluctuation
in the converter nodes.

00:13:10.037 --> 00:13:11.834
It's a minor adjustment.
It's minor.

00:13:11.872 --> 00:13:14.773
It's all right here
on this diagram, Commander.

00:13:17.478 --> 00:13:19.343
Hmm... I'll look
this over later.

00:13:19.379 --> 00:13:21.404
Go ahead... you run
your diagnostic.

00:13:21.448 --> 00:13:23.313
I'll inform
the other departments

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:25.147
about the, uh... power systems.

00:13:26.186 --> 00:13:27.414
I'll check that.

00:13:27.454 --> 00:13:29.888
He's full of energy today.

00:13:29.957 --> 00:13:31.185
I can't get him to slow down.

00:13:31.225 --> 00:13:33.216
He's been working like
that since last night.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:37.094
It looks like a plasma conduit
cut out in junction 17.

00:13:37.131 --> 00:13:38.359
I'll go look at it.

00:13:38.398 --> 00:13:40.889
Wait a minute, Reg,
I'll go with you.

00:13:40.934 --> 00:13:43.266
Keep you posted.

00:13:52.012 --> 00:13:54.572
Computer,
increase ambient temperature

00:13:54.615 --> 00:13:56.276
by two degrees centigrade

00:13:56.316 --> 00:13:59.547
and increase relative humidity
by ten percent.

00:13:59.586 --> 00:14:03.352
Computer, reset environmental
controls to standard.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.858
Worf, it's freezing in here.

00:14:05.926 --> 00:14:08.156
You have already raised
the temperature three times.

00:14:08.195 --> 00:14:09.662
It is too hot.

00:14:09.696 --> 00:14:11.163
Live with it.

00:14:11.198 --> 00:14:13.098
Computer,
execute my original command.

00:14:18.906 --> 00:14:20.373
I need a bath.

00:14:20.407 --> 00:14:22.307
You have the Bridge.

00:14:24.444 --> 00:14:25.877
Here we are.

00:14:25.946 --> 00:14:27.880
Looks like a ruptured conduit.

00:14:27.948 --> 00:14:29.415
No problem.

00:14:29.449 --> 00:14:31.417
I'll just bypass it.

00:14:34.454 --> 00:14:36.183
Reg, wait a second here.

00:14:36.223 --> 00:14:39.624
Take a look at these
corroded edges here.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.629
It looks like something
has dissolved the bulkhead

00:14:42.663 --> 00:14:44.631
and eaten right through
the conduit.

00:14:44.665 --> 00:14:47.395
There are high levels
of cholic acid here...

00:14:47.434 --> 00:14:48.628
enzymatic agents.

00:14:48.669 --> 00:14:50.637
You know, I wouldn't
be surprised

00:14:50.671 --> 00:14:53.196
if that solvent was organic.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.207
Maybe we should run

00:14:54.241 --> 00:14:55.902
a biospectral analysis
on the solvent.

00:14:55.943 --> 00:14:56.910
Take a closer look.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.409
That's a very good idea.

00:14:58.445 --> 00:14:59.844
But first...

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.280
we should take a break.

00:15:02.316 --> 00:15:03.783
You go ahead, sir.

00:15:03.817 --> 00:15:05.250
I'll take care of it.

00:15:05.352 --> 00:15:08.344
Commander, we received
a communication from Starfleet.

00:15:08.388 --> 00:15:09.855
They wanted to know

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.858
when they could expect
your performance analysis

00:15:11.892 --> 00:15:13.860
of the new weapon systems.

00:15:13.894 --> 00:15:15.361
The weapon systems?

00:15:15.395 --> 00:15:17.192
Yes, sir.

00:15:17.231 --> 00:15:21.327
The ones we've been testing
for the past few days?

00:15:21.368 --> 00:15:23.666
That's right.

00:15:25.339 --> 00:15:28.206
What should I tell them... sir?

00:15:28.242 --> 00:15:29.903
Tell them...

00:15:35.415 --> 00:15:37.713
tell them
we haven't finished yet.

00:15:49.429 --> 00:15:51.397
What are you doing here?

00:15:51.431 --> 00:15:53.831
I had to be near you.

00:15:53.867 --> 00:15:57.428
Computer, increase temperature
by five degrees.

00:15:57.471 --> 00:15:59.905
Get out of that water now!

00:15:59.973 --> 00:16:00.962
Leave me alone!

00:16:10.851 --> 00:16:13.217
Could I have a glass of water?

00:16:13.253 --> 00:16:14.845
It's so cold in here.

00:16:14.888 --> 00:16:17.413
Your temperature has dropped
almost eight degrees.

00:16:17.457 --> 00:16:20.426
I want to run a hypothalamic
series right away.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.428
Doctor, we've had
three other crew members

00:16:22.462 --> 00:16:24.430
complaining
about the temperature levels.

00:16:24.464 --> 00:16:26.432
Some feel like they have fevers.

00:16:26.466 --> 00:16:28.434
Others... they're freezing
like Counselor Troi.

00:16:28.468 --> 00:16:30.436
Call Dr. Selar and Dr. Hacopian.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:31.869
It looks like we've
got some sort

00:16:31.905 --> 00:16:33.634
of viral infection
going on around here.

00:16:33.674 --> 00:16:35.232
I want to check
on Lieutenant Worf.

00:16:43.517 --> 00:16:46.975
Worf, have you had any
unusual symptoms lately?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.317
Headaches? Nausea?

00:16:48.355 --> 00:16:50.016
Dizziness?

00:16:50.057 --> 00:16:51.786
Worf?

00:16:51.825 --> 00:16:53.918
Worf, do you hear me?

00:16:55.629 --> 00:16:57.153
I'm going to run a full bioscan.

00:16:57.197 --> 00:16:58.357
I want you to lie down.

00:17:01.401 --> 00:17:04.336
Okay, we can do this sitting up.

00:17:07.708 --> 00:17:10.370
What is this?

00:17:13.714 --> 00:17:17.582
Worf, how long have you
had this on your neck?

00:17:19.753 --> 00:17:23.211
It looks like it's full
of some bioacidic compound...

00:17:23.256 --> 00:17:25.451
almost like a venom sac.

00:17:25.492 --> 00:17:27.619
Worf...

00:17:29.563 --> 00:17:31.690
open your mouth.

00:17:35.635 --> 00:17:37.728
Oh! Oh!

00:17:41.975 --> 00:17:43.442
Get a hypospray.

00:17:43.477 --> 00:17:44.842
Right away.

00:17:48.882 --> 00:17:53.342
I managed to get her into stasis
before the venom paralyzed her.

00:17:53.387 --> 00:17:55.355
She's going to need
reconstructive surgery

00:17:55.389 --> 00:17:57.857
but I-I think
she'll be all right.

00:17:57.891 --> 00:17:59.859
Sir, we've analyzed the venom

00:17:59.893 --> 00:18:02.293
and compared it
to the acidic compound

00:18:02.329 --> 00:18:04.524
found at junction 17
and on decks ten and 12.

00:18:04.564 --> 00:18:06.794
They all have the same
enzymatic composition.

00:18:06.833 --> 00:18:08.664
You're saying that Worf
is spraying this...?

00:18:08.702 --> 00:18:09.691
Venom.

00:18:09.736 --> 00:18:11.533
This venom all over the ship?

00:18:11.571 --> 00:18:13.368
I'd say so.

00:18:13.407 --> 00:18:16.501
60 crewmen have begun exhibiting
strange behavioral changes...

00:18:16.543 --> 00:18:19.376
memory loss, fatigue,
headaches...

00:18:19.413 --> 00:18:22.007
I think one thing is clear.

00:18:22.049 --> 00:18:24.677
There's some sort of disease
aboard the Enterprise...

00:18:24.718 --> 00:18:26.982
and it's spreading.

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:29.955
I'm having trouble
concentrating myself.

00:18:31.158 --> 00:18:33.626
It's like
my mind keeps wandering.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.355
I...

00:18:35.395 --> 00:18:36.692
can't...

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:38.459
Commander, I've got
seven security teams

00:18:38.498 --> 00:18:40.295
out hunting for Worf,
but for some reason

00:18:40.333 --> 00:18:42.096
the sensors are having
a difficult time

00:18:42.135 --> 00:18:43.500
Iocking on to him.

00:18:43.537 --> 00:18:46.506
I've called for a
level-2 security alert.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.168
Do you think we should
go to a level-1?

00:18:49.209 --> 00:18:50.870
I don't know.
What do you think?

00:18:50.977 --> 00:18:52.444
I think we should.

00:18:52.479 --> 00:18:54.208
Okay, sounds good.

00:18:54.247 --> 00:18:57.876
Then you'll take care
of that... security thing?

00:18:57.984 --> 00:19:00.043
Yes, sir, I will.

00:19:00.087 --> 00:19:02.453
Okay. I'll notify Starfleet.

00:19:02.489 --> 00:19:04.582
I'll let them know
what's happening.

00:19:04.624 --> 00:19:06.148
You have your orders.

00:19:07.227 --> 00:19:08.717
Dismissed.

00:19:14.801 --> 00:19:17.668
Computer,
send a subspace message.

00:19:17.704 --> 00:19:21.970
Starfleet Command.
Security channel.

00:19:22.008 --> 00:19:23.942
Authorization...

00:19:23.977 --> 00:19:26.605
Alpha-four-seven authorization
required

00:19:26.646 --> 00:19:29.547
to activate security channel.

00:19:31.084 --> 00:19:33.075
Computer...

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:36.021
Awaiting authorization.

00:19:44.229 --> 00:19:45.821
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:19:45.864 --> 00:19:48.594
Commander Data and I have
recovered the stray torpedo

00:19:48.634 --> 00:19:50.295
after a three-day search.

00:19:50.335 --> 00:19:52.565
We are en route back
to the Enterprise.

00:19:52.604 --> 00:19:56.870
Captain, the ship is not
at the prearranged coordinates.

00:19:58.877 --> 00:20:00.344
Have they been delayed?

00:20:00.379 --> 00:20:01.676
I do not know.

00:20:01.713 --> 00:20:05.308
I am unable to raise them
on any communication channel.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:06.647
Scan the vicinity.

00:20:06.685 --> 00:20:08.744
See if you can find them.

00:20:08.787 --> 00:20:12.348
I found it, sir...
two light-years away.

00:20:12.391 --> 00:20:13.722
Set a course.

00:20:23.835 --> 00:20:26.702
The Enterprise
appears to be adrift.

00:20:26.738 --> 00:20:30.640
I am reading power fluctuations
on all decks.

00:20:30.676 --> 00:20:31.904
Life signs?

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.534
There are life signs.

00:20:33.578 --> 00:20:36.570
However, sensor readings
are highly distorted.

00:20:36.615 --> 00:20:39.448
I am unable to identify
specific life-forms.

00:20:39.484 --> 00:20:41.384
Adjust the axial stabilizers

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.150
to match the attitude
and rotation rate

00:20:44.189 --> 00:20:45.486
of the Enterprise.

00:20:45.524 --> 00:20:48.254
I'm going to dock
the shuttle manually.

00:21:42.481 --> 00:21:44.039
Main power is off-line.

00:21:44.082 --> 00:21:47.108
All systems are in standby
or emergency mode.

00:21:47.152 --> 00:21:50.178
There is no response
from any manned station.

00:21:50.222 --> 00:21:52.190
Any sign of the crew?

00:21:52.224 --> 00:21:54.886
I cannot access internal
sensors from here.

00:21:54.926 --> 00:21:56.985
We will have to go
to the Bridge.

00:22:08.573 --> 00:22:10.404
That sounds like animals.

00:22:10.442 --> 00:22:11.739
Yes, sir.

00:22:11.777 --> 00:22:15.838
I am able to discern over 300
different vocalizations.

00:22:23.422 --> 00:22:25.356
Look at this.

00:22:36.768 --> 00:22:39.328
It is composed of reptilian DNA.

00:22:39.371 --> 00:22:42.135
I believe it is
an epidermal layer

00:22:42.174 --> 00:22:45.268
that has been cast off
during molting.

00:22:45.310 --> 00:22:47.676
But it seems to be...

00:22:47.712 --> 00:22:48.906
humanoid.

00:22:49.014 --> 00:22:51.073
Yes, sir.
I cannot explain it.

00:22:51.116 --> 00:22:54.085
There are no species
aboard the Enterprise

00:22:54.119 --> 00:22:57.020
that shed their skin
in this fashion.

00:23:06.598 --> 00:23:09.192
Sir.

00:23:09.234 --> 00:23:11.862
Hmm.

00:23:11.903 --> 00:23:14.929
These are Counselor Troi's
quarters.

00:23:16.942 --> 00:23:19.410
Can you tell if she's inside?

00:23:19.444 --> 00:23:20.741
No, sir.

00:23:20.779 --> 00:23:25.409
Data, I want to have
a look in here.

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:26.917
Stand ready.

00:23:34.392 --> 00:23:35.689
Whew...

00:23:35.727 --> 00:23:38.560
Environmental settings
in these quarters

00:23:38.597 --> 00:23:40.087
have been altered.

00:23:47.172 --> 00:23:49.140
Data, over here.

00:24:04.156 --> 00:24:05.282
Deanna...

00:24:05.323 --> 00:24:06.756
What's happened to her?

00:24:10.195 --> 00:24:13.460
Her DNA is in a state
of ribocyatic flux.

00:24:13.498 --> 00:24:15.966
Her genetic codes
are being re-sequenced

00:24:16.001 --> 00:24:19.562
and her cells are mutating
as a result.

00:24:19.604 --> 00:24:23.631
At a fundamental level, sir,
she is no longer human.

00:24:23.675 --> 00:24:25.142
What is she?

00:24:25.177 --> 00:24:27.771
Her respiratory tissue
has become capable

00:24:27.812 --> 00:24:29.973
of metabolizing
both water and air

00:24:30.015 --> 00:24:33.382
and her eyes have developed
nictitating membranes.

00:24:33.418 --> 00:24:35.648
I believe she is amphibian, sir.

00:24:35.687 --> 00:24:38.155
She has been injured.

00:24:40.158 --> 00:24:42.126
Yes, sir.

00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:44.355
There is Klingon DNA
in the wound.

00:24:44.396 --> 00:24:45.693
It is saliva.

00:24:45.730 --> 00:24:48.460
Are you saying
she's been bitten?

00:24:48.500 --> 00:24:51.094
It would appear so.

00:24:53.405 --> 00:24:56.670
I will need to run
a full biospectral analysis.

00:24:58.743 --> 00:25:02.645
First, we've got to get
the ship under control.

00:25:02.681 --> 00:25:04.672
Let's go to the Bridge.

00:25:28.907 --> 00:25:31.671
His upper spinal column
has been broken in three places.

00:25:31.710 --> 00:25:34.611
It looks as though he's been
attacked by an animal.

00:25:34.646 --> 00:25:36.045
Yes, sir.

00:25:36.081 --> 00:25:38.140
Has his DNA been changed,
as well?

00:25:38.183 --> 00:25:40.617
Yes, sir.

00:25:40.652 --> 00:25:44.816
However, it was in its
initial stages when he died.

00:25:56.368 --> 00:25:58.359
Captain...

00:26:02.140 --> 00:26:04.836
I am picking up 1,011
individual life-forms

00:26:04.943 --> 00:26:06.240
within the ship.

00:26:06.278 --> 00:26:08.610
All exhibit
a similar genetic flux

00:26:08.647 --> 00:26:11.514
to the one we observed
in Counselor Troi.

00:26:11.549 --> 00:26:14.518
So, the entire ship
has been affected.

00:26:14.552 --> 00:26:15.849
Most of the life-forms

00:26:15.954 --> 00:26:18.013
are scattered
throughout the ship.

00:26:18.056 --> 00:26:20.957
However, there are several
large concentrations

00:26:20.992 --> 00:26:23.256
in the arboretum
and the aquatic lab.

00:26:23.295 --> 00:26:25.855
I've regained attitude
control to the ship

00:26:25.964 --> 00:26:28.296
but main power
is still off-line.

00:26:28.333 --> 00:26:29.630
It looks as though

00:26:29.668 --> 00:26:32.762
the entire power transfer grid
has been destroyed.

00:27:08.473 --> 00:27:10.441
Will?

00:27:16.681 --> 00:27:18.444
Captain.

00:27:21.820 --> 00:27:24.846
His cranial plates
have thickened by 20%.

00:27:24.889 --> 00:27:28.450
His brain
is much smaller, sir.

00:27:28.493 --> 00:27:30.586
I do not believe he can
comprehend our language.

00:27:31.629 --> 00:27:33.859
Perhaps we can find
a way to communicate.

00:27:33.965 --> 00:27:35.296
Will, can you

00:27:35.333 --> 00:27:37.164
understand what it is
that I'm...?

00:27:53.852 --> 00:27:55.877
He looks almost protohuman.

00:27:55.987 --> 00:27:57.284
Yes, sir.

00:27:57.322 --> 00:28:01.656
His DNA would seem
to confirm that observation.

00:28:01.693 --> 00:28:05.629
Captain, I believe
the crew is de-evolving.

00:28:15.740 --> 00:28:17.833
This tranquilizer
should keep him unconscious

00:28:17.908 --> 00:28:19.967
for another seven hours.

00:28:22.446 --> 00:28:24.346
What have you found out?

00:28:24.382 --> 00:28:29.649
I have analyzed
Commander Riker's DNA structure.

00:28:29.687 --> 00:28:32.952
A synthetic T cell has
invaded his genetic codes.

00:28:32.990 --> 00:28:36.517
This T cell has begun
to activate his latent introns.

00:28:36.560 --> 00:28:37.993
Introns?

00:28:38.028 --> 00:28:41.862
They are genetic codes
which are normally dormant.

00:28:41.966 --> 00:28:44.867
They are evolutionary
holdovers...

00:28:44.969 --> 00:28:47.563
sequences of DNA
which provided

00:28:47.605 --> 00:28:50.130
key behavioral and
physical characteristics

00:28:50.174 --> 00:28:53.143
millions of years ago,
but are no longer necessary.

00:28:53.177 --> 00:28:56.340
For instance, Counselor
Troi's gill slits

00:28:56.380 --> 00:28:58.746
and other amphibious
characteristics

00:28:58.783 --> 00:29:00.512
were derived from introns

00:29:00.551 --> 00:29:02.781
which still contain
amphibious codes.

00:29:02.820 --> 00:29:06.449
So, these introns
are causing her DNA

00:29:06.490 --> 00:29:09.152
to recombine
in an earlier configuration.

00:29:09.193 --> 00:29:10.421
That is correct.

00:29:10.461 --> 00:29:14.158
In her case, the DNA has created
an amphibious life-form

00:29:14.198 --> 00:29:17.599
which became extinct
over 50 million years ago.

00:29:17.635 --> 00:29:20.627
And Commander Riker's introns

00:29:20.671 --> 00:29:22.400
are changing him
into what appears

00:29:22.440 --> 00:29:24.169
to be
one of the earlier hominids.

00:29:24.208 --> 00:29:25.300
Yes, sir.

00:29:25.342 --> 00:29:27.173
I would say australopithecine.

00:29:29.613 --> 00:29:31.843
Each of these stages
is another link

00:29:31.882 --> 00:29:33.315
in the evolutionary chain

00:29:33.350 --> 00:29:34.749
which stretches back
to the origins

00:29:34.785 --> 00:29:36.753
of all life-forms on Earth.

00:29:36.787 --> 00:29:40.348
Because introns can
include genetic material

00:29:40.391 --> 00:29:42.052
from many different species

00:29:42.092 --> 00:29:44.356
over millions
of years of evolution

00:29:44.395 --> 00:29:45.555
it is possible

00:29:45.596 --> 00:29:47.655
that a wide variety
of transformations

00:29:47.698 --> 00:29:48.858
is occurring among the crew.

00:29:48.966 --> 00:29:51.434
What about those crew members
who are not from Earth?

00:29:51.469 --> 00:29:54.802
All humanoid life has
a similar genetic pattern.

00:29:54.839 --> 00:29:57.831
The virus should work
on nonhuman crew members

00:29:57.875 --> 00:29:59.536
in the same way.

00:29:59.577 --> 00:30:02.705
They are each de-evolving
into earlier forms of life

00:30:02.746 --> 00:30:04.304
on their homeworlds.

00:30:04.348 --> 00:30:07.545
I feel I must inform you, sir.

00:30:07.585 --> 00:30:11.487
You have also been infected
by the intron virus.

00:30:14.225 --> 00:30:17.058
How long
before I begin to change?

00:30:17.094 --> 00:30:20.086
According to my calculations,
within the next 12 hours

00:30:20.130 --> 00:30:22.428
you will begin to exhibit
the first signs

00:30:22.466 --> 00:30:24.798
of your eventual transformation.

00:30:26.804 --> 00:30:29.637
And what will that be?

00:30:29.673 --> 00:30:32.369
I believe
you will also de-evolve

00:30:32.409 --> 00:30:34.900
into an earlier form of primate

00:30:35.012 --> 00:30:38.914
possibly similar to a lemur
or pygmy marmoset.

00:30:45.122 --> 00:30:47.056
Well...

00:30:47.091 --> 00:30:49.889
before I begin swinging
through the ship

00:30:49.927 --> 00:30:51.394
Iooking for breakfast

00:30:51.428 --> 00:30:53.362
we'd better find some answers.

00:30:53.397 --> 00:30:55.490
How do we reverse the process?

00:30:55.533 --> 00:30:56.830
I am uncertain.

00:30:56.867 --> 00:31:00.234
We will need to run
several micro-cellular scans.

00:31:00.271 --> 00:31:03.707
However, the ship's
main computer has been damaged.

00:31:03.741 --> 00:31:06.209
Captain, the computer
in my quarters

00:31:06.243 --> 00:31:09.974
has an independent processing
and memory storage unit.

00:31:10.014 --> 00:31:12.107
It should not
have been affected.

00:31:12.149 --> 00:31:14.014
I suggest we start from there.

00:31:14.051 --> 00:31:15.416
Agreed.

00:31:32.736 --> 00:31:36.069
It would appear
that Spot has had her kittens.

00:31:43.881 --> 00:31:45.348
They sound hungry.

00:31:45.382 --> 00:31:46.849
Yes.

00:31:46.884 --> 00:31:50.615
I am curious as to why
Spot is not caring for them.

00:31:58.929 --> 00:32:01.193
It would seem
that the intron virus

00:32:01.231 --> 00:32:03.791
is not limited
to humanoid life-forms.

00:32:03.834 --> 00:32:05.597
No, sir.

00:32:13.310 --> 00:32:15.778
What is it?

00:32:15.813 --> 00:32:19.510
These kittens were born
less than 24 hours ago.

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:22.883
It would appear that
Spot's transformation took place

00:32:22.920 --> 00:32:25.889
at approximately
the same time.

00:32:25.923 --> 00:32:28.221
So, Spot was giving birth
to the kittens

00:32:28.258 --> 00:32:29.657
at the same time

00:32:29.693 --> 00:32:32.253
that she was changing
into a reptilian life-form.

00:32:32.296 --> 00:32:34.764
I believe so.

00:32:34.798 --> 00:32:37.198
For some reason,
the intron virus

00:32:37.234 --> 00:32:38.667
was not passed on
to the kittens.

00:32:38.702 --> 00:32:40.693
I do not know why.

00:32:42.806 --> 00:32:44.068
If I remember my biology

00:32:44.108 --> 00:32:46.235
there are several
natural immune systems

00:32:46.276 --> 00:32:48.369
that come into play
in the mother's womb

00:32:48.412 --> 00:32:50.710
to protect the fetus
from viral infections.

00:32:50.748 --> 00:32:52.045
That is true.

00:32:52.082 --> 00:32:54.482
Placental barriers,
maternal antibodies

00:32:54.518 --> 00:32:55.917
and amniotic fluids

00:32:55.953 --> 00:32:58.114
all serve
as a filtration system.

00:32:58.155 --> 00:33:01.124
Maybe we could have inhibited
the intron virus

00:33:01.158 --> 00:33:04.719
by using the natural antibodies
in Spot's amniotic fluid.

00:33:04.762 --> 00:33:06.696
It would take further research

00:33:06.730 --> 00:33:10.359
but I believe to be effective
on humanoid crew members

00:33:10.401 --> 00:33:12.995
humanoid antibodies
would be necessary.

00:33:13.037 --> 00:33:15.562
Then we should locate
a pregnant humanoid.

00:33:15.606 --> 00:33:18.097
Nurse Ogawa has recently
become pregnant.

00:33:18.142 --> 00:33:19.302
Where is she?

00:33:21.679 --> 00:33:24.079
I have traced
her combadge signal

00:33:24.114 --> 00:33:26.207
to deck 17, section 21 alpha.

00:33:26.250 --> 00:33:27.615
The arboretum.

00:33:29.787 --> 00:33:32.278
One of the warp plasma vents
has failed.

00:33:32.322 --> 00:33:34.290
Main Engineering
has been abandoned.

00:33:34.324 --> 00:33:36.656
There is no one there
to fix the problem.

00:33:44.134 --> 00:33:47.126
I can repair the damaged
plasma vent from here.

00:33:47.171 --> 00:33:50.971
I'm going to check the status
of the warp core.

00:34:26.810 --> 00:34:28.107
Data!

00:34:30.647 --> 00:34:32.114
What was that?

00:34:35.052 --> 00:34:37.520
I believe it was
Lieutenant Barclay.

00:34:37.554 --> 00:34:40.148
He appeared
to be partially transformed

00:34:40.190 --> 00:34:41.589
into an arachnid.

00:34:41.625 --> 00:34:43.286
A spider?

00:34:43.327 --> 00:34:44.692
Yes, sir.

00:34:44.728 --> 00:34:47.754
Are you all right, Captain?

00:34:47.798 --> 00:34:51.894
I have these
intense feelings of...

00:34:51.969 --> 00:34:54.597
fear...

00:34:54.638 --> 00:34:57.732
and panic.

00:34:57.775 --> 00:34:59.572
I feel as if I were
being watched.

00:34:59.610 --> 00:35:00.907
I can't...

00:35:00.944 --> 00:35:02.241
I can't explain it.

00:35:02.279 --> 00:35:03.644
You may be experiencing

00:35:03.680 --> 00:35:06.148
the initial stages
of your transformation.

00:35:06.183 --> 00:35:08.845
Early primates were often prey
to large carnivores.

00:35:08.886 --> 00:35:11.150
As a result, their instincts
probably included

00:35:11.188 --> 00:35:13.053
a heightened sense
of awareness.

00:35:13.090 --> 00:35:14.557
In that case

00:35:14.591 --> 00:35:18.220
my instincts tell me
that we'd better hurry.

00:35:33.043 --> 00:35:35.011
Captain...

00:35:35.045 --> 00:35:37.138
I have analyzed
Nurse Ogawa's embryo.

00:35:37.181 --> 00:35:39.149
It is unaffected by the virus.

00:35:39.183 --> 00:35:41.708
I believe I can use
her amniotic fluid

00:35:41.752 --> 00:35:43.879
as a template for a retrovirus.

00:35:43.921 --> 00:35:46.583
It would neutralize
the synthetic T cell

00:35:46.623 --> 00:35:49.888
and reestablish the genetic
patterns of each host.

00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:51.257
How soon can you do that?

00:35:51.295 --> 00:35:52.853
It will not take long

00:35:52.896 --> 00:35:54.887
to isolate the appropriate
genetic material.

00:35:54.932 --> 00:35:57.457
I will need to get
the Sick Bay computer back on...

00:36:01.738 --> 00:36:02.602
What was that?

00:36:05.542 --> 00:36:07.373
It is large.

00:36:07.410 --> 00:36:10.072
Approximately 200 kilograms.

00:36:10.113 --> 00:36:14.106
It is heavily armored
with an exoskeleton.

00:36:14.150 --> 00:36:17.950
Life signs appear
to be Klingon.

00:36:17.988 --> 00:36:20.081
Worf.

00:36:34.371 --> 00:36:36.862
Set your phaser on heavy stun.

00:36:36.973 --> 00:36:38.873
We can't be certain
the stun setting

00:36:38.908 --> 00:36:40.432
will have any effect on him.

00:36:40.477 --> 00:36:42.274
A higher setting might kill him.

00:36:43.380 --> 00:36:45.405
Listen to that.

00:36:45.448 --> 00:36:47.075
He sounds very angry...

00:36:47.117 --> 00:36:49.881
really... really aggressive.

00:36:49.953 --> 00:36:51.887
What do you think he wants?

00:36:51.988 --> 00:36:54.889
Do you think
he's responding to some...

00:36:54.991 --> 00:36:57.050
some predatory instinct?

00:36:58.928 --> 00:37:01.362
Do you think he sees us as prey?

00:37:01.398 --> 00:37:03.389
There are crew members
in the corridors

00:37:03.433 --> 00:37:05.094
and other sections of the ship.

00:37:05.135 --> 00:37:06.534
It would be easier for him

00:37:06.569 --> 00:37:08.400
to capture
and consume one of them

00:37:08.438 --> 00:37:10.599
than to attempt
to break through a door.

00:37:14.544 --> 00:37:17.035
Then what does he want?

00:37:17.080 --> 00:37:22.575
Predators use vocalizations
to frighten other predators

00:37:22.619 --> 00:37:25.554
and to mark territory...

00:37:25.588 --> 00:37:31.686
and to commence mating process.

00:37:31.728 --> 00:37:33.821
A mating process...

00:37:35.465 --> 00:37:37.262
Counselor Troi
was bitten by a Klingon

00:37:37.300 --> 00:37:39.495
but not in a place
that might be life-threatening.

00:37:39.536 --> 00:37:42.505
Nowhere near a major artery
or organ.

00:37:42.539 --> 00:37:44.564
Data, look at this.

00:37:44.607 --> 00:37:46.074
Look at this injury.

00:37:46.109 --> 00:37:48.407
This wound was never intended

00:37:48.445 --> 00:37:51.437
to give her
any kind of serious harm.

00:37:51.481 --> 00:37:53.711
Captain,
what are you suggesting?

00:37:53.750 --> 00:37:57.345
Is it possible that Worf could
see Counselor Troi as his mate?

00:37:57.387 --> 00:38:01.346
If that is true, he must
be trying to reach her now.

00:38:01.391 --> 00:38:02.915
Well, we can't just leave.

00:38:02.959 --> 00:38:04.984
We have to stay here
and protect her.

00:38:05.028 --> 00:38:07.622
And we have to keep on working
on the retrovirus.

00:38:07.664 --> 00:38:09.131
If we could distract him.

00:38:09.165 --> 00:38:11.395
If we could lure him away
from her...

00:38:11.434 --> 00:38:13.664
The mating instinct
is quite strong

00:38:13.703 --> 00:38:15.000
in Klingon biology.

00:38:15.038 --> 00:38:18.132
I am not certain
what would be an effective lure.

00:38:18.174 --> 00:38:21.007
Klingons have got
a very powerful sense of smell.

00:38:21.044 --> 00:38:23.444
If we could duplicate
Deanna's pheromones

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:26.108
and then convince him
that she's no longer in Sick Bay

00:38:26.149 --> 00:38:29.482
that she'd gone into some
other part of the ship...

00:38:32.489 --> 00:38:36.585
I am extracting a blood sample
from one of her sebaceous glands

00:38:36.626 --> 00:38:38.890
where the pheromones
are produced.

00:38:44.567 --> 00:38:47.161
I believe I can activate
the pheromones

00:38:47.203 --> 00:38:49.137
with a bioactivant solution.

00:38:49.172 --> 00:38:50.867
Can you amplify the pheromones?

00:38:50.940 --> 00:38:52.874
They need to be
much more powerful

00:38:52.942 --> 00:38:54.466
than Deanna's actual scent.

00:38:54.511 --> 00:38:57.036
I believe this will produce
the desired effect.

00:38:57.080 --> 00:39:00.140
I will use it to draw Worf
to another part of the ship.

00:39:00.183 --> 00:39:02.413
No, no, no. You must go on
working on the retrovirus.

00:39:02.452 --> 00:39:03.612
I'll go.

00:39:03.653 --> 00:39:05.814
Captain, that is
extremely unwise.

00:39:05.855 --> 00:39:07.254
Worf may be faster...

00:39:07.290 --> 00:39:09.258
No time...
no time to argue.

00:40:32.141 --> 00:40:33.904
Deck 17.

00:40:34.010 --> 00:40:35.375
Deck 17!

00:40:59.302 --> 00:41:03.466
Computer, display progress
of genetic re-sequencing.

00:41:24.827 --> 00:41:28.092
Genetic re-sequencing
in progress.

00:41:28.131 --> 00:41:30.224
DNA to 70% normal.

00:41:30.266 --> 00:41:35.260
Computer, increase nucleotide
substitution by 32%.

00:42:10.106 --> 00:42:12.040
Data to Captain Picard.

00:42:12.075 --> 00:42:13.474
Go ahead, Data.

00:42:13.509 --> 00:42:15.739
The retrovirus is working, sir.

00:42:15.778 --> 00:42:18.838
I can release it into the ship's
atmosphere in a gaseous state.

00:42:18.881 --> 00:42:21.611
However, it will take some time
to take effect.

00:42:21.651 --> 00:42:23.016
Acknowledged!

00:42:23.052 --> 00:42:25.486
Are you all right, sir?

00:42:25.521 --> 00:42:28.046
Yes, I'm fine, Mr. Data.

00:42:28.091 --> 00:42:30.457
Proceed.

00:42:33.529 --> 00:42:35.622
Well, Mr. Worf...

00:42:35.665 --> 00:42:41.797
let's hope that when you wake up
you're a new man.

00:42:41.838 --> 00:42:44.136
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:44.173 --> 00:42:47.870
Commander Data has succeeded in
returning the crew to normal.

00:42:47.910 --> 00:42:49.502
Dr. Crusher has determined

00:42:49.545 --> 00:42:51.536
that the synthetic T cell
she used

00:42:51.581 --> 00:42:53.606
to cure
Mr. Barclay's Urodelean flu

00:42:53.649 --> 00:42:57.050
initiated the intron virus,
which swept through the ship.

00:42:57.086 --> 00:42:59.179
So, this is my fault.

00:42:59.222 --> 00:43:00.746
No.

00:43:00.790 --> 00:43:03.088
In a way, it's mine.

00:43:03.126 --> 00:43:06.061
I didn't realize it at the time

00:43:06.095 --> 00:43:08.359
but there's an anomaly
in your genetic chemistry

00:43:08.398 --> 00:43:11.196
that caused the synthetic
T cell to mutate.

00:43:11.234 --> 00:43:14.203
Instead of activating
one dormant gene

00:43:14.237 --> 00:43:16.330
it started activating
all of them

00:43:16.372 --> 00:43:18.033
including your introns.

00:43:18.074 --> 00:43:20.008
A-And that's what...

00:43:20.043 --> 00:43:23.012
and that's what caused
me to de-evolve?

00:43:23.046 --> 00:43:25.139
You and every other member
of the crew.

00:43:25.181 --> 00:43:27.149
The T cell became airborne

00:43:27.183 --> 00:43:28.980
and started to spread
like a virus.

00:43:29.018 --> 00:43:33.455
You know, Reg, this is
a completely new disease

00:43:33.489 --> 00:43:35.821
and it's traditional
to classify a new disease

00:43:35.858 --> 00:43:38.019
with the name of the first
diagnosed patient.

00:43:38.061 --> 00:43:40.029
Oh, you mean

00:43:40.063 --> 00:43:43.897
you want to name
the disease after me?

00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:45.024
That's right.

00:43:45.068 --> 00:43:47.059
How about "Barclay's
Protomorphosis Syndrome"?

00:43:47.103 --> 00:43:49.537
"Barclay's Protomorphosis..."

00:43:49.572 --> 00:43:51.267
Um, well...

00:43:51.307 --> 00:43:53.537
It has a nice ring to it.

00:43:53.576 --> 00:43:55.771
Thank you, Doctor.

00:43:58.614 --> 00:44:00.343
He transformed into a spider

00:44:00.383 --> 00:44:03.011
and now he has a disease
named after him.

00:44:03.052 --> 00:44:05.646
I think I better
clear my calendar

00:44:05.688 --> 00:44:07.553
for the next few weeks.
